  icon: {fileID: 2800000, guid: b332f069270551048ae90f30573ba746, type: 3}
  title: Chapter 01<br>Unity basics and 3D physics
  sections:
  - heading: 'Part 01: Anatomy of a scene'
    text: Scenes are a specific kind of asset where the game logic happens. Understanding
      how scenes work and their relation to the project view is important to understand
      how to work in Unity.
    links:
    - linkText: Read on the GameObject-Component relationship
      url: https://docs.unity3d.com/520/Documentation/Manual/TheGameObject-ComponentRelationship.html
    - linkText: How to use Components
      url: https://docs.unity3d.com/520/Documentation/Manual/UsingComponents.html
    - linkText: On the difference between a Script and a Component
      url: https://docs.unity3d.com/520/Documentation/Manual/TheComponent-ScriptRelationship.html
    icon: {fileID: 2800000, guid: ae1c96d73d1679c43a836f06adc3b437, type: 3}
    scene: {fileID: 102900000, guid: e15120d5197a89148b86bbb545afb63a, type: 3}
    checkList: []
  - heading: Exercises
    text: To understand Unity's approach to scenes and assets I've prepared a series
      of small exercises. Use the knowledge you've gathered from the example scene
      and the previous and following links to complete them.
    links:
    - linkText: Types of properties in a Component
      url: https://docs.unity3d.com/520/Documentation/Manual/EditingValueProperties.html
    - linkText: Scene View navigation (pertinent to Exercise 1)
      url: https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.1/Documentation/Manual/SceneViewNavigation.html
    - linkText: More info on how to use the Scene View
      url: https://docs.unity3d.com/520/Documentation/Manual/UsingTheSceneView.html
